From 433efed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dineshr93 <dineshr93@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add --sbom to write a protobom SBOM at configure time

---
diff --git a/docs/markdown/Commands.md b/docs/markdown/Commands.md
index 8369313..9645d5e 100644
--- a/docs/markdown/Commands.md
+++ b/docs/markdown/Commands.md
@@ -286,6 +286,14 @@ as `meson configure <builddir> -Dopt=value`.
 *Since 1.3.0* It is possible to clear the cache and reconfigure in a single command
 with `meson setup --clearcache --reconfigure <builddir>`.
 
+*Since 1.13.0* `--sbom` writes a [protobom](https://github.com/protobom/protobom)
+SBOM of the configured project to `<builddir>/sbom.protobom.bin`. The document
+lists every configured target and its resolved dependencies, with a
+`pkg:generic/<name>@<version>` purl where the project version is known. It is
+generated at configure time, so it contains no artifact hashes, and Meson does
+not model a supplier or per-target license, so those fields are omitted. The
+output is deterministic when `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` is set.
+
 {{ setup_arguments.inc }}
 
 See [Meson introduction
diff --git a/docs/markdown/snippets/sbom.md b/docs/markdown/snippets/sbom.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..804990e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/markdown/snippets/sbom.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+## SBOM generation
+
+`meson setup --sbom` now writes a [protobom](https://github.com/protobom/protobom)
+SBOM of the configured project to `<builddir>/sbom.protobom.bin`. The document
+lists every configured target and its resolved dependencies, with a
+`pkg:generic/<name>@<version>` purl where the project version is known.
+
+The SBOM is generated at configure time, so it contains no artifact hashes.
+Meson does not model a supplier or a per-target license, so those fields are
+omitted. The output is deterministic when `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` is set.
